            "review_text": "無名\nWorld9941 contributions\n0\nSomething's missing...\nDec 2017 • Solo\n...and I think it's some flavor. I had six pieces of nigiri (sake [salmon], ebi, tomago) and some sort of deep-fried roll that was supposed to be tuna but I ain't so sure of that. The sake was kind of limp and the tomago wasn't really yellow. This place was real busy probably because prices were really reasonable. All that for about 140000 VND. Oh yea, potato salad too. I guess I shouldn't complain. I didn't really walk away unhappy - just resentful I didn't go to some places I saw along the walk back to the hotel.\nRead more\nWritten December 14, 2017",
